1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,131
Most people know the Toyota 2000GT as

2
00:00:03,131 --> 00:00:06,008
the Japanese car from a James Bond

3
00:00:06,008 --> 00:00:06,431
film.

4
00:00:06,611 --> 00:00:08,765
Far fewer know how it started,

5
00:00:08,765 --> 00:00:11,062
or what it cost the company that

6
00:00:11,062 --> 00:00:11,708
built it.

7
00:00:11,888 --> 00:00:14,432
Here are two things you probably did

8
00:00:14,432 --> 00:00:16,763
not know about the Toyota 2000GT,

9
00:00:16,763 --> 00:00:18,035
and along the way,

10
00:00:18,035 --> 00:00:21,072
every place where our sources disagree with

11
00:00:21,072 --> 00:00:21,850
each other.

12
00:00:22,199 --> 00:00:25,676
Our sources are Wikipedia's pages on the

13
00:00:25,676 --> 00:00:28,892
Toyota 2000GT, the Nissan S30 and the

14
00:00:28,892 --> 00:00:32,282
Nissan Z-car, Classic and Sports Car on

15
00:00:32,282 --> 00:00:35,325
the twenty twenty-two Gooding sale,

16
00:00:35,325 --> 00:00:37,671
Hagerty, Sports Car Market,

17
00:00:37,671 --> 00:00:41,844
Shannons Club and Luxury Entertainment Partners.

18
00:00:42,024 --> 00:00:43,489
Where they conflict,

19
00:00:43,489 --> 00:00:45,100
we show both versions.

20
00:00:45,280 --> 00:00:48,345
Our own arithmetic is always labelled.

21
00:00:48,696 --> 00:00:50,836
The first thing you probably did not

22
00:00:50,836 --> 00:00:52,680
know is that Toyota was not the

23
00:00:52,680 --> 00:00:54,524
first company offered this car.

24
00:00:54,704 --> 00:00:57,645
Wikipedia's page on the Nissan Z says

25
00:00:57,645 --> 00:00:59,951
Nissan partnered with Yamaha,

26
00:00:59,951 --> 00:01:03,369
which produced a prototype called the YX-30

27
00:01:03,369 --> 00:01:05,118
in nineteen sixty-one.

28
00:01:05,298 --> 00:01:07,094
By nineteen sixty-four,

29
00:01:07,094 --> 00:01:08,187
the page says,

30
00:01:08,187 --> 00:01:10,685
Nissan had scrapped the project.

31
00:01:11,035 --> 00:01:14,018
The reason, according to that same page,

32
00:01:14,018 --> 00:01:17,225
was that Yamaha's twin-cam two litre engine

33
00:01:17,225 --> 00:01:19,835
did not meet Nissan's expectations.

34
00:01:20,015 --> 00:01:22,929
Yamaha then took the design to Toyota.

35
00:01:23,109 --> 00:01:26,020
The result, says Wikipedia,

36
00:01:26,020 --> 00:01:28,392
was the Toyota 2000GT.

37
00:01:28,572 --> 00:01:31,296
So the car that became Japan's first

38
00:01:31,296 --> 00:01:34,247
supercar began as a design that another

39
00:01:34,247 --> 00:01:37,198
Japanese carmaker had walked away from.

40
00:01:37,548 --> 00:01:39,417
The story has a second layer.

41
00:01:39,597 --> 00:01:42,956
The Shannons Club article says Nissan hired

42
00:01:42,956 --> 00:01:44,518
a German aristocrat,

43
00:01:44,518 --> 00:01:47,720
Albrecht Goertz, as a consultant from May

44
00:01:47,720 --> 00:01:49,361
nineteen sixty-three.

45
00:01:49,541 --> 00:01:53,164
He built a Nissan prototype called the

46
00:01:53,164 --> 00:01:57,168
A550X, with many styling themes later seen

47
00:01:57,168 --> 00:01:58,980
on the Datsun 240Z.

48
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:02,045
It says Goertz then moved to Toyota

49
00:02:02,045 --> 00:02:04,105
and developed the 2000GT.

50
00:02:04,456 --> 00:02:06,740
Our sources do not tell this story

51
00:02:06,740 --> 00:02:07,613
the same way.

52
00:02:07,793 --> 00:02:12,319
The Hagerty article says Yamaha's A550X concept

53
00:02:12,319 --> 00:02:14,533
was rejected by Nissan,

54
00:02:14,533 --> 00:02:17,711
and that Toyota also passed on it

55
00:02:17,711 --> 00:02:20,503
at first, but saw Yamaha as a

56
00:02:20,503 --> 00:02:24,547
possible partner, which led to the 2000GT.

57
00:02:24,727 --> 00:02:27,940
The Wikipedia page on the Toyota 2000GT

58
00:02:27,940 --> 00:02:30,659
does not mention Goertz at all in

59
00:02:30,659 --> 00:02:32,389
the passages we read.

60
00:02:32,740 --> 00:02:34,603
So there are three versions of the

61
00:02:34,603 --> 00:02:35,096
handover.

62
00:02:35,276 --> 00:02:38,836
In one, Nissan scrapped Yamaha's project,

63
00:02:38,836 --> 00:02:41,093
and Yamaha went to Toyota.

64
00:02:41,273 --> 00:02:43,839
In another, Goertz himself moved.

65
00:02:44,019 --> 00:02:44,896
In a third,

66
00:02:44,896 --> 00:02:46,572
Toyota first said no,

67
00:02:46,572 --> 00:02:47,769
then came back.

68
00:02:47,949 --> 00:02:50,544
They are not necessarily contradictory,

69
00:02:50,544 --> 00:02:52,940
but none of our sources explains how

70
00:02:52,940 --> 00:02:54,138
they fit together,

71
00:02:54,138 --> 00:02:56,002
and we will not guess at the

72
00:02:56,002 --> 00:02:56,401
order.

73
00:02:56,751 --> 00:02:59,128
What the sources agree on is the

74
00:02:59,128 --> 00:02:59,723
outcome.

75
00:02:59,903 --> 00:03:03,303
Shannons says Toyota sold few 2000GTs but

76
00:03:03,303 --> 00:03:07,035
gained publicity, and that this pushed Nissan

77
00:03:07,035 --> 00:03:10,932
to take the Goertz prototype toward production.

78
00:03:11,112 --> 00:03:14,205
The Wikipedia page on the S30 says

79
00:03:14,205 --> 00:03:17,388
the same thing from the other side:

80
00:03:17,388 --> 00:03:21,754
the 2000GT's success prompted Nissan to continue

81
00:03:21,754 --> 00:03:24,483
developing its own sports car,

82
00:03:24,483 --> 00:03:26,484
which became the 240Z.

83
00:03:26,834 --> 00:03:28,145
The dates support that.

84
00:03:28,325 --> 00:03:31,846
Wikipedia says the Toyota 2000GT was shown

85
00:03:31,846 --> 00:03:34,779
at the Tokyo Motor Show in nineteen

86
00:03:34,779 --> 00:03:38,803
sixty-five, and production ran from May nineteen

87
00:03:38,803 --> 00:03:42,072
sixty-seven to August nineteen seventy.

88
00:03:42,252 --> 00:03:44,903
The Datsun 240Z was shown at the

89
00:03:44,903 --> 00:03:47,969
Tokyo Motor Show on the eighteenth of

90
00:03:47,969 --> 00:03:50,288
October nineteen sixty-nine,

91
00:03:50,288 --> 00:03:51,365
per Shannons.

92
00:03:51,545 --> 00:03:53,040
By our arithmetic,

93
00:03:53,040 --> 00:03:56,113
that is four years after the 2000GT's

94
00:03:56,113 --> 00:03:57,525
first appearance.

95
00:03:57,875 --> 00:03:59,616
There is one more detail.

96
00:03:59,796 --> 00:04:01,754
Wikipedia says Yamaha,

97
00:04:01,754 --> 00:04:04,603
the motorcycle and engine maker,

98
00:04:04,603 --> 00:04:07,807
built the 2000GT cars at its factory

99
00:04:07,807 --> 00:04:10,744
at Iwata, in Shizuoka prefecture.

100
00:04:10,924 --> 00:04:13,180
So the car sold under a Toyota

101
00:04:13,180 --> 00:04:16,113
badge was assembled by a company better

102
00:04:16,113 --> 00:04:17,767
known for motorcycles,

103
00:04:17,767 --> 00:04:20,700
using a design that Nissan had dropped.

104
00:04:20,880 --> 00:04:22,592
That is the first thing most people

105
00:04:22,592 --> 00:04:23,179
do not know.

106
00:04:23,529 --> 00:04:25,944
The second thing you probably did not

107
00:04:25,944 --> 00:04:27,903
know is that the car that made

108
00:04:27,903 --> 00:04:30,319
Toyota look like a serious sports car

109
00:04:30,319 --> 00:04:32,213
maker lost the company money.

110
00:04:32,393 --> 00:04:35,582
Wikipedia's page says that only about sixty

111
00:04:35,582 --> 00:04:37,584
cars reached North America,

112
00:04:37,584 --> 00:04:40,180
and that Toyota made no profit from

113
00:04:40,180 --> 00:04:40,996
the 2000GT.

114
00:04:41,176 --> 00:04:42,998
The car was a statement,

115
00:04:42,998 --> 00:04:44,136
not a business.

116
00:04:44,487 --> 00:04:46,639
The plan was far larger than the

117
00:04:46,639 --> 00:04:47,110
result.

118
00:04:47,290 --> 00:04:48,935
Classic and Sports Car,

119
00:04:48,935 --> 00:04:52,438
writing about the twenty twenty-two Gooding sale,

120
00:04:52,438 --> 00:04:55,083
says Toyota hoped to build a thousand

121
00:04:55,083 --> 00:04:55,941
cars a year,

122
00:04:55,941 --> 00:04:58,371
but in the end built three hundred

123
00:04:58,371 --> 00:04:59,086
fifty-one.

124
00:04:59,266 --> 00:05:02,117
Production ran for about three and a

125
00:05:02,117 --> 00:05:03,225
quarter years.

126
00:05:03,405 --> 00:05:04,515
By our arithmetic,

127
00:05:04,515 --> 00:05:06,489
a thousand a year over that time

128
00:05:06,489 --> 00:05:08,956
would have been about three thousand two

129
00:05:08,956 --> 00:05:10,127
hundred fifty cars.

130
00:05:10,478 --> 00:05:11,756
By our arithmetic,

131
00:05:11,756 --> 00:05:14,880
three hundred fifty-one cars is about eleven

132
00:05:14,880 --> 00:05:17,223
percent of that hoped-for volume.

133
00:05:17,403 --> 00:05:18,706
Or put another way,

134
00:05:18,706 --> 00:05:21,107
one year of the original plan would

135
00:05:21,107 --> 00:05:23,781
have been nearly three times the entire

136
00:05:23,781 --> 00:05:24,810
production run.

137
00:05:24,990 --> 00:05:27,473
The sources do not say whether the

138
00:05:27,473 --> 00:05:29,736
thousand a year was a target on

139
00:05:29,736 --> 00:05:33,022
paper, or something Toyota actually tooled up

140
00:05:33,022 --> 00:05:33,314
for.

141
00:05:33,665 --> 00:05:36,486
The count of cars is itself disputed.

142
00:05:36,666 --> 00:05:41,188
Wikipedia's infobox gives three hundred fifty-one,

143
00:05:41,188 --> 00:05:44,895
split into two hundred thirty-three MF10,

144
00:05:44,895 --> 00:05:48,242
one hundred nine MF10L and nine MF12L

145
00:05:48,242 --> 00:05:48,694
cars.

146
00:05:48,874 --> 00:05:51,828
But its text says three hundred thirty-seven

147
00:05:51,828 --> 00:05:53,506
regular production units.

148
00:05:53,686 --> 00:05:57,017
Sports Car Market says three hundred fifty-four

149
00:05:57,017 --> 00:05:57,796
were built.

150
00:05:57,976 --> 00:06:00,298
Neither page reconciles the figures.

151
00:06:00,648 --> 00:06:02,010
By our arithmetic,

152
00:06:02,010 --> 00:06:05,719
the spread between three hundred thirty-seven and

153
00:06:05,719 --> 00:06:08,973
three hundred fifty-four is seventeen cars,

154
00:06:08,973 --> 00:06:10,412
about five percent.

155
00:06:10,592 --> 00:06:13,691
The left-hand-drive count is also contested.

156
00:06:13,871 --> 00:06:18,767
Sports Car Market's table lists eighty-four left-hand-drive

157
00:06:18,767 --> 00:06:21,755
cars, while its text says sixty-two.

158
00:06:21,935 --> 00:06:26,360
Luxury Entertainment Partners also describes a car

159
00:06:26,360 --> 00:06:29,458
as one of sixty-two US-market cars.

160
00:06:29,808 --> 00:06:31,439
Why would a company make a car

161
00:06:31,439 --> 00:06:33,070
it could not sell at a profit?

162
00:06:33,250 --> 00:06:34,748
The price gives a clue.

163
00:06:34,928 --> 00:06:38,019
Wikipedia says the 2000GT cost about seven

164
00:06:38,019 --> 00:06:41,036
thousand one hundred fifty dollars in the

165
00:06:41,036 --> 00:06:43,832
United States in nineteen sixty-eight.

166
00:06:44,012 --> 00:06:46,823
Sports Car Market gives an original list

167
00:06:46,823 --> 00:06:49,353
price of six thousand eight hundred.

168
00:06:49,533 --> 00:06:51,538
We cannot tell which is right,

169
00:06:51,538 --> 00:06:53,542
or whether one is a base price

170
00:06:53,542 --> 00:06:55,547
and the other a delivered one.

171
00:06:55,897 --> 00:06:59,786
Wikipedia puts the 2000GT's price in context.

172
00:06:59,966 --> 00:07:02,109
In nineteen sixty-eight,

173
00:07:02,109 --> 00:07:05,592
a Jaguar E-Type cost five thousand five

174
00:07:05,592 --> 00:07:08,093
hundred thirty-nine dollars,

175
00:07:08,093 --> 00:07:11,754
a Porsche 911S six thousand seven hundred

176
00:07:11,754 --> 00:07:15,327
ninety, and a Ferrari 365 GTB/4 nineteen

177
00:07:15,327 --> 00:07:17,381
thousand seven hundred.

178
00:07:17,561 --> 00:07:18,934
By our arithmetic,

179
00:07:18,934 --> 00:07:22,367
the Toyota cost twenty-nine percent more than

180
00:07:22,367 --> 00:07:25,190
the Jaguar and five percent more than

181
00:07:25,190 --> 00:07:26,106
the Porsche.

182
00:07:26,456 --> 00:07:28,012
Against the Ferrari,

183
00:07:28,012 --> 00:07:29,880
the picture is reversed.

184
00:07:30,060 --> 00:07:31,507
By our arithmetic,

185
00:07:31,507 --> 00:07:34,801
the 2000GT cost thirty-six percent of the

186
00:07:34,801 --> 00:07:38,014
Ferrari's price, so the Ferrari cost two

187
00:07:38,014 --> 00:07:40,103
point eight times as much.

188
00:07:40,283 --> 00:07:43,571
Toyota priced its car above the Jaguar

189
00:07:43,571 --> 00:07:46,599
and Porsche but well below Ferrari.

190
00:07:46,779 --> 00:07:49,319
The sources do not say how Toyota

191
00:07:49,319 --> 00:07:50,627
chose that price,

192
00:07:50,627 --> 00:07:53,013
or what each car cost to build.

193
00:07:53,363 --> 00:07:55,490
So the second thing most people do

194
00:07:55,490 --> 00:07:57,430
not know is the gap between the

195
00:07:57,430 --> 00:07:58,681
image and the books.

196
00:07:58,861 --> 00:08:00,802
The car looked like a triumph,

197
00:08:00,802 --> 00:08:02,355
and it later became one.

198
00:08:02,535 --> 00:08:03,685
But at the time,

199
00:08:03,685 --> 00:08:05,338
according to Wikipedia,

200
00:08:05,338 --> 00:08:07,493
Toyota earned nothing from it.

201
00:08:07,673 --> 00:08:09,852
The profit, if you want to call

202
00:08:09,852 --> 00:08:11,258
it that, came later,

203
00:08:11,258 --> 00:08:13,297
and it went to the people who

204
00:08:13,297 --> 00:08:14,351
owned the cars,

205
00:08:14,351 --> 00:08:15,336
not to Toyota.

206
00:08:15,685 --> 00:08:18,243
To understand why anyone wanted it,

207
00:08:18,243 --> 00:08:19,412
look at the car.

208
00:08:19,592 --> 00:08:22,417
Wikipedia lists a length of four thousand

209
00:08:22,417 --> 00:08:24,966
one hundred seventy-five millimetres,

210
00:08:24,966 --> 00:08:26,826
a width of sixteen hundred,

211
00:08:26,826 --> 00:08:29,237
and a height of only eleven hundred

212
00:08:29,237 --> 00:08:31,993
sixty, with a two thousand three hundred

213
00:08:31,993 --> 00:08:33,164
thirty wheelbase.

214
00:08:33,344 --> 00:08:36,119
It weighed eleven hundred twenty kilograms.

215
00:08:36,469 --> 00:08:38,944
The engine was a one thousand nine

216
00:08:38,944 --> 00:08:42,510
hundred eighty-eight cubic centimetre inline six,

217
00:08:42,510 --> 00:08:43,528
called the 3M.

218
00:08:43,708 --> 00:08:46,694
Wikipedia says it started from the block

219
00:08:46,694 --> 00:08:48,859
of the Toyota Crown's engine,

220
00:08:48,859 --> 00:08:51,845
with a twin-cam head developed by Yamaha

221
00:08:51,845 --> 00:08:55,353
and three two-barrel Mikuni-Solex carburettors.

222
00:08:55,533 --> 00:08:58,746
So even the engine was a collaboration,

223
00:08:58,746 --> 00:09:01,547
a Toyota block with a Yamaha head.

224
00:09:01,897 --> 00:09:04,698
It made a hundred fifty metric horsepower

225
00:09:04,698 --> 00:09:06,475
at sixty-six hundred revs,

226
00:09:06,475 --> 00:09:09,959
which Wikipedia converts to one hundred forty-eight

227
00:09:09,959 --> 00:09:13,853
horsepower, and one hundred seventy-five newton-metres of

228
00:09:13,853 --> 00:09:15,493
torque at five thousand.

229
00:09:15,673 --> 00:09:18,465
Sports Car Market says one hundred fifty

230
00:09:18,465 --> 00:09:20,839
horsepower at seven thousand revs.

231
00:09:21,019 --> 00:09:22,328
By our arithmetic,

232
00:09:22,328 --> 00:09:25,746
that is about seventy-six metric horsepower per

233
00:09:25,746 --> 00:09:29,018
litre, and one hundred thirty-four per tonne.

234
00:09:29,368 --> 00:09:32,046
Wikipedia gives a claimed top speed of

235
00:09:32,046 --> 00:09:34,723
one hundred thirty-five miles an hour,

236
00:09:34,723 --> 00:09:36,413
and says it was a claim,

237
00:09:36,413 --> 00:09:38,950
with the figure tied to a particular

238
00:09:38,950 --> 00:09:39,725
axle ratio.

239
00:09:39,905 --> 00:09:43,153
It also claims thirty-one miles per gallon,

240
00:09:43,153 --> 00:09:45,570
and gives no zero to sixty time.

241
00:09:45,750 --> 00:09:48,749
Classic and Sports Car mentions an early

242
00:09:48,749 --> 00:09:51,597
development car, Project two eighty A,

243
00:09:51,597 --> 00:09:54,971
at a hundred forty-eight brake horsepower and

244
00:09:54,971 --> 00:09:57,894
one hundred thirty-seven miles an hour.

245
00:09:58,244 --> 00:10:00,868
The top speed itself is disputed.

246
00:10:01,048 --> 00:10:03,961
Wikipedia says one hundred thirty-five,

247
00:10:03,961 --> 00:10:06,873
Classic and Sports Car says one hundred

248
00:10:06,873 --> 00:10:09,188
thirty-seven for the prototype,

249
00:10:09,188 --> 00:10:12,922
and Luxury Entertainment Partners says one hundred

250
00:10:12,922 --> 00:10:13,668
forty-six.

251
00:10:13,848 --> 00:10:15,272
By our arithmetic,

252
00:10:15,272 --> 00:10:18,040
the spread is eleven miles an hour.

253
00:10:18,220 --> 00:10:20,580
None of the three says who measured

254
00:10:20,580 --> 00:10:22,401
it, so we treat them all as

255
00:10:22,401 --> 00:10:24,559
claims rather than test results.

256
00:10:24,908 --> 00:10:26,963
It was not only a show car.

257
00:10:27,143 --> 00:10:29,769
Wikipedia lists a third place at the

258
00:10:29,769 --> 00:10:32,612
nineteen sixty-six Japanese Grand Prix,

259
00:10:32,612 --> 00:10:35,383
a win at the nineteen sixty-six Suzuka

260
00:10:35,383 --> 00:10:37,134
one thousand kilometres,

261
00:10:37,134 --> 00:10:39,977
and wins in nineteen sixty-seven at the

262
00:10:39,977 --> 00:10:42,821
Fuji twenty-four hours and the Fuji one

263
00:10:42,821 --> 00:10:44,280
thousand kilometres.

264
00:10:44,460 --> 00:10:46,964
The car was entered in real races

265
00:10:46,964 --> 00:10:48,558
in its first seasons.

266
00:10:48,908 --> 00:10:53,133
Wikipedia also describes a speed-record attempt at

267
00:10:53,133 --> 00:10:55,583
Yatabe in nineteen sixty-six,

268
00:10:55,583 --> 00:10:58,963
saying the car broke thirteen records in

269
00:10:58,963 --> 00:11:00,484
seventy-two hours.

270
00:11:00,664 --> 00:11:03,605
Our sources do not give the individual

271
00:11:03,605 --> 00:11:05,230
records, the drivers,

272
00:11:05,230 --> 00:11:06,314
or the speeds,

273
00:11:06,314 --> 00:11:09,023
so we can report the headline only.

274
00:11:09,203 --> 00:11:11,818
The page uses the figure seventy-two,

275
00:11:11,818 --> 00:11:13,231
which is three days,

276
00:11:13,231 --> 00:11:15,351
and we have no other source to

277
00:11:15,351 --> 00:11:16,482
compare it with.

